      "submitted_at": "2026-11-12T18:18:41Z",
      "body": "<!-- centaur:sha:b6c6bc68c661d8e2b43996ce213ce9a51b52b7d0 -->\n## Centaur Review\n\nFound **2** issue(s) (2 warning).\n\n### Convergence\n**Recommendation:** `fix` — All blocking findings are new and marked fixable.\n\n- New blocking findings: 2\n- Unresolved blocking findings: 0\n- Non-blocking follow-ups: 0\n- Repeated/deferred findings: 0\n- Verified resolved findings: 0\n\n\n### `server/agent-tool-selection.ts`\n_Two correctness gaps remain in skill restriction projection and nested observation validation._\n\n- 🟡 **bugs** (L128) `CEN-960117BA3EF5`: Claude's AskUserQuestion is a native SDK tool, so its skill-policy key is `AskUserQuestion`, not `mcp__mitzo-connections__AskUserQuestion`. With a skill ceiling containing `AskUserQuestion`, this projection incorrectly reports the tool as restricted although the permission handler allows it. Resolve policy names using the actual registration for each helper and cover this case. `[fixable]` `[blocking]`\n\n\n### `frontend/src/components/SessionAccess.tsx`\n_Two correctness gaps remain in skill restriction projection and nested observation validation._\n\n- 🟡 **unsafe_assumptions** (L72) `CEN-51993782E611`: The receipt check validates only the outer readiness session ID. RuntimeReadinessSchema validates shape but does not correlate `capabilities.evidence.scope` with that ID, the observed account/model, or the configured binding. A payload with matching outer IDs and another session's nested observation passes and renders `Succeeded`. Validate these internal relationships before replacing retained evidence, and add a mounted-consumer regression for a mismatched nested scope. `[fixable]` `[blocking]`\n\n\n<!-- centaur:job:dimakis/mitzo:1322:b6c6bc68c661d8e2b43996ce213ce9a51b52b7d0:0 -->",
